2025: LLMs get a gold medal at the IMO Now, GPT-5.6 solves famous frontier math/stat questions. The IMO is today and 5.6 one-shotting a perfect score isn’t even news. Where will we be next year?</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2077762676932165996">https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2077762676932165996</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/saturday-assorted-links-570.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-570">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2077762676932165996</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2077762676932165996</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 15:43:03 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Joel Mokyr on Clans, Corporations, and a Culture of Growth (Ep. 282)]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://conversationswithtyler.com/episodes/joel-mokyr/">https://conversationswithtyler.com/episodes/joel-mokyr/</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-a6a">Economics Links, 7/19/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://conversationswithtyler.com/episodes/joel-mokyr/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://conversationswithtyler.com/episodes/joel-mokyr/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 11:02:36 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[State, Clan, and Liberty - Econlib]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.econlib.org/library/Columns/y2013/Klingclan.html">https://www.econlib.org/library/Columns/y2013/Klingclan.html</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-a6a">Economics Links, 7/19/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.econlib.org/library/Columns/y2013/Klingclan.html</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.econlib.org/library/Columns/y2013/Klingclan.html</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 11:02:36 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Warsh's Challenges, Financial Regu